ốc There are two real numbers \(a\) and \(b\) that satisfy the system of equations:
\[ \left\{
\begin{array}{l}
a^3 - 3a^2 + 5a - 17 = 0, \\
b^3 - 3b^2 + 5b + 11 = 0.
\end{array}
\right. ốc
Find the value of \(a + b\).

Find the smallest non-negative integer \( n \) satisfying \begin{align*}
    3n + 4 &\equiv 7 \pmod{5}, \\
    5n + 3 &\equiv 8 \pmod{4}, \\
    2n + 1 &\equiv 3 \pmod{3}.
\end{align*}\boxed{\phantom{123}}

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv a \pmod{b_1} \\
x \equiv a \pmod{b_2} \\
x \equiv a \pmod{b_3}
\end{cases}
\]
where \( a = 2 \), \( b_1 = 3 \), \( b_2 = 5 \), and \( b_3 = 7 \). What is the value of \( x \)?

Evaluate the limit: \[
\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin(3x) - 3x \cos(x)}{x^3}
\]

The parabolas y = x^2 + 4x + 2 and y = 5 - x^2 intersect. Establish a second condition that interacts with the
problem, such as finding the average x-coordinate across all intersection points. Calculate the average x-coordinate
indicating the point of symmetry for the intersection pair.}

Find the total number of integer solutions \((x, y)\) to the system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x^2 + y^2 \equiv 1 \pmod{11} \\
x - y \equiv 2 \pmod{11}
\end{cases}
\]

A polynomial \( f(x) \) with real coefficients is defined as:
$$f(x) = \begin{cases} 
\frac{e^{x^2-1}-1}{x}, & \text{if } x \neq 0 \\
a, & \text{if } x = 0
\end{cases}$$
Given that \( \lim_{{x \to 0}} f(x) \) exists and equals \( \frac{1}{2} \), determine the value of \( a \).\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}

